  "id": "operant-chamber",
  "term": "operant chamber",
  "definition": "An operant chamber is a laboratory enclosure used to study instrumental behavior by arranging a response, such as pressing a lever, to produce a reward when a set requirement is met. In the supplied study, rats received rewarding brain stimulation in the chamber after enough cumulative lever-press time had been completed.",
